# The toolchain Codometer 1.0.0 is built with. Read by Scripts/release.sh (stage 1, which sources this file)
# and by the two GitHub workflows (which parse it — they never source it). docs/RELEASING.md §6 lists the keys
# the workflows care about and what they do when the runner image does not have the pinned Xcode.
#
# A mismatch is a hard failure in release.sh and in release.yml; ci.yml downgrades it to a visible warning,
# because a runner image drifts faster than a tag does. Override once with --allow-toolchain-mismatch.

# First choice of Xcode on a runner. Without it the workflows look for /Applications/Xcode_<version>.app.
XCODE_APP="/Applications/Xcode_26.6.app"
# Must match the two lines of `xcodebuild -version`.
XCODE_VERSION="26.6"
XCODE_BUILD="17F113"
# `swift --version` reports 6.3.3 with that Xcode; the language mode the package needs is 6.2.
SWIFT_MIN="6.2"

# Keys below here belong to Scripts/release.sh and Scripts/verify-bundle.sh; the workflows ignore them.
MACOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET="26.0"
# Apple silicon only for 1.0.0.
ARCHS="arm64"
CI_RUNNER="macos-26"
